From 2074c84f4f777af6784b2f7765751e7a318886ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Anderson <dvander@google.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Oct 2019 15:11:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add fastbootd to the sys_rawio whitelist.

A similar problem was previously encountered with the boot control HAL
in bug 118011561. The HAL may need access to emmc to implement
set_active commands.

fastbootd uses the boot control HAL in passthru mode when in recovery,
so by extension, it needs this exception as well.

Bug: 140367894
Test: fastbootd can use sys_rawio
Change-Id: I1040e314a58eae8a516a2e999e9d4e2aa51786e7
(cherry picked from commit 1d13a7ed16338bb57e6069a0307d380c706df73b)
---
 prebuilts/api/29.0/private/domain.te | 1 +
 private/domain.te                    | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/prebuilts/api/29.0/private/domain.te b/prebuilts/api/29.0/private/domain.te
index 209eeb0dd00b77ee399dc64c3320cebaf3a7abc1..1d26761d6b7dad5daba9ae653428240b10d05e52 100644
--- a/prebuilts/api/29.0/private/domain.te
+++ b/prebuilts/api/29.0/private/domain.te
@@ -312,4 +312,5 @@ neverallow {
   -uncrypt
   -tee
   -hal_bootctl_server
+  -fastbootd
 } self:global_capability_class_set sys_rawio;
diff --git a/private/domain.te b/private/domain.te
index 209eeb0dd00b77ee399dc64c3320cebaf3a7abc1..1d26761d6b7dad5daba9ae653428240b10d05e52 100644
--- a/private/domain.te
+++ b/private/domain.te
@@ -312,4 +312,5 @@ neverallow {
   -uncrypt
   -tee
   -hal_bootctl_server
+  -fastbootd
 } self:global_capability_class_set sys_rawio;
